        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Plan grouped Claw agent updates",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add `openclaw.clawUpdatePlan.v1` for read-only, agent-centric reconciliation of a grouped Claw manifest\n- add `openclaw claws update <claw-or-agent> [--from <source>] --dry-run [--json]` behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`\n- default the target source from persisted add provenance; `--from` remains an explicit override or recovery path\n- compare agent config, workspace files, exact package refs, source-level MCP declarations, and agent-pinned cron declarations\n- bind the complete preview to `planIntegrity` for the consented apply slice\n- perform no mutation: planning opens existing state read-only, does not create or migrate databases, and closes every owned handle\n\n## Planning contract\n\n- direct agent ids and unambiguous installed package names resolve to one root install record\n- older supported databases without Claws tables return structured `claw_not_found`\n- missing workspaces and owned artifacts are planned for restoration; unsafe roots, operator drift, and incomplete ownership remain blocked\n- blocked actions produce a nonzero CLI result even when no separate diagnostic blocker exists\n- unchanged packages skip add-time preflight; missing artifacts require it; exact Claw-owned plugin upgrades may accept only the expected installed-version conflict\n- independently owned packages and MCP declarations cannot be restored or changed by a Claw\n- removing package refs never mutates drifted artifacts; shared, independently owned, missing, or modified MCP declarations use explicit `release` actions that preserve global config\n- source MCP config is compared before placeholder resolution so credentials and local substitutions do not create false drift\n\n## Verification\n\n- 40 focused update-planner, package, and CLI tests\n- all 8 real Claw lifecycle E2E tests\n- core tsgo typecheck\n- focused Oxlint: 0 warnings and 0 errors\n- Oxfmt and `git diff --check`\n- `codex review --base upstream/user/giodl/claws-pr10-doctor`: no actionable findings\n- read-only regression compares state database bytes and mtime before and after planning\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102427 read-only diagnostics\n- This PR: authoritative read-only update planning and consent boundary\n- Next: #102982 executes only a freshly rebuilt, unblocked, consent-matched plan\n",
